#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725411 :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral CDAB with measurements](images/bf/bf86dd66e68aa803862e9d743bff40c2c4e507b1504cd854e998c43b67babb59.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ is $6\\,\\text{in}^{2}$. The sides $CD=4.5\\,\\text{in}$ and $CB=9\\,\\text{in}$ meet at $110^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle DAB$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $CDB$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDB}&=\\frac12\\cdot CD\\cdot CB\\cdot\\sin\\angle DCB\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 4.5\\cdot 9\\cdot\\sin110^\\circ\\\\&\\approx19.028776\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ and the missing triangle $DAB$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAB}&=A_{CDB}-A_{CDAB}\\\\&=20.25\\sin110^\\circ-6\\\\&\\approx13.028776\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $13\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725419 :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral BCDA with measurements](images/b0/b08362b6e0a41d7a1860dcb0e37152640d1262e9270714e8748b3f3ddc3081af.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $BCDA$ is $4\\,\\text{in}^{2}$. The sides $BC=7\\,\\text{in}$ and $BA=5\\,\\text{in}$ meet at $52^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle CDA$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $BCA$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{BCA}&=\\frac12\\cdot BC\\cdot BA\\cdot\\sin\\angle CBA\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 7\\cdot 5\\cdot\\sin52^\\circ\\\\&\\approx13.790188\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $BCDA$ and the missing triangle $CDA$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDA}&=A_{BCA}-A_{BCDA}\\\\&=17.5\\sin52^\\circ-4\\\\&\\approx9.790188\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $10\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725421 :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral CDAB with measurements](images/40/40e1a732a1fa15bb08da6ed21d1df3da4d15b87cef3daf6bdcdd548aa2f303bf.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ is $6\\,\\text{in}^{2}$. The sides $CD=5\\,\\text{in}$ and $CB=9\\,\\text{in}$ meet at $42^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle DAB$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $CDB$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDB}&=\\frac12\\cdot CD\\cdot CB\\cdot\\sin\\angle DCB\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 5\\cdot 9\\cdot\\sin42^\\circ\\\\&\\approx15.055439\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ and the missing triangle $DAB$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAB}&=A_{CDB}-A_{CDAB}\\\\&=22.5\\sin42^\\circ-6\\\\&\\approx9.055439\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $9\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725424 :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral DABC with measurements](images/85/859e1b1de8f994f597260f539c60411b175e652084a628e7e196d0236c1b31fe.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $DABC$ is $7\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$. The sides $DA=9\\,\\text{cm}$ and $DC=4\\,\\text{cm}$ meet at $70^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $DAC$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAC}&=\\frac12\\cdot DA\\cdot DC\\cdot\\sin\\angle ADC\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 9\\cdot 4\\cdot\\sin70^\\circ\\\\&\\approx16.914467\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $DABC$ and the missing triangle $ABC$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{ABC}&=A_{DAC}-A_{DABC}\\\\&=18\\sin70^\\circ-7\\\\&\\approx9.914467\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $10\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$."}]}
